The conditions laid down therein are as follows:
"i)Driving Test for the post of Drivers;
ii)Efficiency Test (Issuing tickets in line) for the post of Conductor;
iii)Physical fitness including Eye test, Hearing Test and Tolerance Test;
iv)They should be non-alcoholic and without any bad habits;
v)Before appointing, their antecedent report should be obtained to ensure that they are fully suitable for the post;
vi)They will be appointed on Daily paid category as per existing practice in the Corporation."
10.Besides this G.O., Rule 11(2) of the Common Service Rules framed for the transport corporation was also pressed into service, wherein it was stated that the candidate should possess sound health,
active habits and should free from any bodily defect or deformity.

